# Fantasy Friends — environment configuration
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in your own project's values.
# `.env.local` is git-ignored; never commit real keys.
#
# Vite only exposes variables that start with VITE_, and it INLINES them into the
# published JavaScript bundle. That makes the two rules below non-negotiable:
#
#   1. NEVER put the service_role key in a VITE_ variable. It bypasses every RLS
#      policy and would give anyone who opens your site full database access. The
#      app actively refuses to start if it detects one (src/lib/supabase.ts).
#   2. Only the anon / publishable key belongs here. It is safe in a browser
#      because every table is protected by RLS and the only callable database
#      surface is the reviewed ff_* RPC set.
#
# Leave both values empty to run in Demo mode: the app stores everything in this
# browser, needs no account, and makes no network calls.

# Project URL, e.g. https://<your-project-ref>.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=

# The anon (publishable) key from Project Settings -> API.
# Legacy form is a long JWT starting "eyJ..."; new form starts "sb_publishable_".
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build-time only (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Base path for the deployed site. GitHub Pages project sites need "/<repo>/".
# VITE_BASE_PATH=/Hagz-fantasy/

# "hash" for GitHub Pages (no server-side rewrite available), unset for normal hosts.
# VITE_ROUTER_MODE=hash
